1
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,400
My name is Manuel. I travel to listen
to the people nobody usually listens to,

2
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,200
and let them be the ones
to tell their own lives.

3
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,600
My mission is to give a voice
to those who need it most.

4
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,400
This is Voci Vere.

5
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:48,600
It's seven in the morning and these people
have been walking since midnight,

6
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:53,000
13 kilometres along the coast of Kerala,
praying the rosary without ever stopping.

7
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,000
Hundreds of thousands of people.

8
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:58,100
The first time, in 2002,
there were only a few hundred.

9
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,400
It starts from a shrine dedicated to Mary,
in Kalavoor,

10
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,700
for thirteen, fourteen kilometres
all the way to Arthunkal.

11
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,600
It's a walk that happens every year.

12
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,800
It comes from an apparition of Mary,

13
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,000
here in Alappuzha.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,800
About four hundred thousand people take part.

15
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,600
In Kerala, Christianity is ancient.

16
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:21,600
It's said to have arrived in 52 AD
with the apostle Thomas.

17
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,300
It's like a prayer to Jesus, my love.

18
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,800
Why do you come back every year?

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,400
For the Mother, Mary.

20
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:30,900
We always come.

21
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:32,900
There are Christians...

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:33,900
Yes.

23
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:34,900
Muslims.

24
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Yes. All together.

25
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:44,600
A whole community
giving out water and food.

26
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:48,900
Some pray, some watch from their homes,
some hand out water, some are just curious.

27
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,500
Volunteers, men and women,
devoted to the cause.

28
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,400
Hindu volunteers lending a hand,
even though it's a Catholic festival.

29
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,500
Truly a community coming together.

30
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,700
This was a stop
for a drink and a bite to eat.

31
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:06,800
Let's try to join them for a little while,
respecting the tradition.

32
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,900
They used to do it all on the road,
then the traffic made it too chaotic

33
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:18,000
and they moved straight onto the beach.

34
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,800
It's an act of devotion to Our Lady.

35
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,200
She has given me many blessings in my life.

36
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,200
I'm twenty-six.

37
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,800
It's my first time here.

38
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:32,800
Is it your first time?

39
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:33,800
No.

40
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,800
We walked on the beach.

41
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,300
And now we're on the road.

42
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:38,900
What does it mean to you?

43
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,400
It's faith, it's believing.

44
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,400
Many miracles happen there.

45
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:46,300
Whoever takes part finds something.

46
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,500
A bit of happiness.

47
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,600
And after kilometres of walking...

48
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,600
We've arrived.

49
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,300
The church was rebuilt
by an Italian Jesuit in 1584.

50
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,000
Father Giacomo Fenicio.

51
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:14,200
Here they still call him Veluthachan,
the white father.

52
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:19,700
In 1647 a statue of Saint Sebastian arrives,
to be kept in the church.

53
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:27,900
It's boiling hot, so humid.

54
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:41,400
The journey of Voci Vere, giving a voice
to those who need it most, continues.

55
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,600
Follow me to discover the next stories.

